Subject: Carry compiled calls and returns between compiled activations

What this does
  Adds the engine side of the AOT unit's fifth round: a compiled function can
  now return without an interpreter activation, call another compiled function
  on a light frame or on the caller's C stack, fold a numeric constant-pool
  operand, and read `this` itself. The generated prologue reads the frame and
  bytecode fields it needs through offsets instead of five cross-unit accessor
  calls.

Why we need it
  A compiled call still cost an interpreter activation: the callee ran on a
  light frame but the return went back through the threaded dispatcher, so a
  call could not be a plain C call. Measured on the two microbenchmarks, calls
  were 38 ns each and box2d's compiled loops spent most of their time in
  per-call frame setup. The unit also could not express a return, a constant
  taken from the function's pool, or `this` as a value, so those ops left
  compiled code and disabled their function.

What it adds
  REGVM_FLAG_C_ENTRY and REGVM_C_RET
                            - a light frame entered from compiled code returns
                              its value to the C frame that entered it instead
                              of tail-calling into a caller's dispatch; the
                              return, typed return and unwind handlers all
                              honour it
  regvm_light_fill          - the fill split out of regvm_light_enter so a frame
                              entered from compiled code is built by the same
                              code the interpreter's light call path uses, with
                              the receiver passed in
  qjs_aot_call_light        - the arena path for a compiled callee
  qjs_aot_call_leaf         - the same call with the callee's frame in the
                              caller's stack buffer; declines a callee that is
                              already its own ancestor so deep recursion still
                              raises RangeError instead of faulting
  REGVM_FLAG_STACK          - marks that stack frame, so a light frame its
                              interpreted remainder calls is taken from the
                              arena top rather than laid after it on the C
                              stack; the call seals an arena caller first, as
                              qjs_aot_call_light does
  regvm_light_apply_arguments
                            - the light-frame `f.apply(this, arguments)` path,
                              shared by the threaded handler and the step
                              handler `qjs_aot_step` runs; the step handler
                              had only the record form, which reads `argv`
                              and the JSStackFrame a light frame does not have
  regvm_aot_run_to_end      - finishes a C-entered activation in the threaded
                              interpreter from a resume pc, used by deopt and by
                              an uncaught throw
  qjs_aot_return            - a compiled return: moves the value out of its
                              register with its own DRC reference
  qjs_aot_binary_cpool      - `a <op> const` for a constant-pool or atom operand
  qjs_aot_this              - the receiver as a value, boxed for a non-strict
                              function exactly as the interpreter's handler does
  qjs_aot_gv_gen            - the global-slot generation an inline global-read
                              hit compares against
  js_aot_gen_layout         - JSRegRun and JSFunctionBytecode field offsets, the
                              runtime's cell generation, the context's
                              interrupt counter and runtime, and the function
                              object's bytecode field, all covered by the
                              layout hash
  JSAotGenFunc              - the numeric constant-pool entries, so the
                              generator folds a pooled constant into a C
                              literal; and the light-frame size a direct call
                              needs
  js_aot_gen_free           - takes the element count, and releases each
                              function's pool copy

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

Notes
  Only offsets are shared with the unit, never a size: JSRegRun differs between
  the QJS_AOT and QJS_AOT_GEN builds and the layout hash must not depend on
  that. js_aot_gen_free is generator-only and not part of the unit ABI, so its
  signature change needs no bump either; a stale unit fails to bind on the
  layout hash. Deep compiled recursion on a stack frame is refused when the
  callee is already an ancestor, which is what keeps the interpreter's
  RangeError.

